    "b-kg2-drift-lede": {
      "id": "b-kg2-drift-lede",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The drift gate is the librarian's counterpart of the worker quality gate — a pass over a subject is not done until every code citation the flagger marked drifted or unresolvable has been re-cited, rewritten, or cleared."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-kg2-drift-where-h": {
      "id": "b-kg2-drift-where-h",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Where it runs"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-kg2-drift-where-reconcile": {
      "id": "b-kg2-drift-where-reconcile",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Rename continuity in report reconciliation — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge-v2/ingest/reconcile.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It runs whenever the checkout head moves: boundary sync pulls upstream PRs, or an epoch boundary integrates our own worker outputs. Within a unit, it pairs one newly unresolved symbol with one newly inserted symbol at the same address. Pairing is 1:1 and requires the same kind. It marks the old row moved with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "target.moved_to_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " from migration 005, then re-points facts, evidence, links, worker runs, pull requests, events, and the index stamp. Ambiguous addresses appear in the reconcile result and remain unchanged. Reconciliation never enqueues tasks."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-kg2-drift-where-flagger": {
      "id": "b-kg2-drift-where-flagger",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The flagger — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge-v2/drift/flagger.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "flagCodeDrift",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". It re-resolves each "
        },
        {
          "insert": "code://",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " citation's path and span at the current head, recomputes the digest, and classifies the citation as unchanged, drifted, or unresolvable. The operation is deterministic and read-only."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-kg2-drift-where-context": {
      "id": "b-kg2-drift-where-context",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Context assembly — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge-v2/librarian/context.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr_imported",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "run_closed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " contexts carry two fields per touched subject: "
        },
        {
          "insert": "renamed_from",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", containing stable keys of rows whose "
        },
        {
          "insert": "moved_to_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " points at it, and the compact drift report. These are the two live pathways. They do not create a separate drift task."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-kg2-drift-where-gate": {
      "id": "b-kg2-drift-where-gate",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The gate — apps/server/src/core/knowledge-v2/librarian/consumer.ts. It runs only when the context carried drift inputs (the builder sets drift_gate for pr_imported, run_closed, and drift_recheck); Discord archival passes and backfill passes skip it and complete as before, because no code changed. When gated: after applyLibrarianPass it runs the flagger again on the touched subjects. A clean result completes the task. Drift left on the first attempt releases the task with drift_attempts=1 so the queue re-claims it once. Drift left on the second attempt completes the task anyway and logs 'drift left unresolved after retry' in the pass artifact. The artifact records drift_gate as skipped, clean, released, or warned."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-kg2-drift-where-scan": {
      "id": "b-kg2-drift-where-scan",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The manual scan — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "kg2-drift-scan",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "apps/server/src/core/knowledge-v2/drift/cli.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Use it after a large upstream jump. It flags the whole store and enqueues one "
        },
        {
          "insert": "drift_recheck",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " task per unit, deduplicated against pending tasks. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "drift_recheck",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the only pathway this job uses."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
